tion/math-academy-id "q-149564" :question/problem "| **Number of Members ($x$)** | $3$ | $4$ | $4$ | $5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **Number of Cars ($y$)** | $2$ | $2$ | $2$ | $6$ |\n\nIn a survey of $4$ families, the number of members in each family was recorded as well as the number of cars owned by that family. The data is shown in the table above.\nCompute the covariance of the data sets given that the means are $\\overset{―}{x}=4$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=3.$" :question/worked-solution "The (population) covariance of the data sets $x={{x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}}$ and $y={{y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n}}$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}(x,y)=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}),\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i}$ are the means of the data sets.\n\nTherefore, the covariance of our data sets is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}(x,y) & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(3-4)(2-3)+(4-4)(2-3)+(4-4)(2-3)+(5-4)(6-3)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(-1)(-1)+(0)(-1)+(0)(-1)+(1)(3)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[1+0+0+3] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-149564/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cee807c1-dd86-5b0e-a595-5c5754c47e4c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-149564"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-149570/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "4a18b879-4571-552b-9fa9-f88a0eef33e5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-149570/selection/d0d01bb2e3e816b9fd6aee47accd74e6df07f3f36fe536db4d7bfbcde2546d68" :answer/id #uuid "5d132bed-0864-5d61-a97e-e36d677d924c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-149570/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer/id #uuid "251ebd13-d55b-500c-a810-b1367a01e8dd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-149570/selection/1b562e91f68bc228d59da280605802cc1ce0248d770285443e7d649fb5c75d13" :answer/id #uuid "27ef66a0-b9ad-58ac-bb9f-b29c9fc5750d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-149570/selection/03a4102f13ad3e0ac65ab53676c3f89cede3c650c4dd4e31a2b43a62847e184f" :answer/id #uuid "72c61957-55ea-58cf-9273-4522b3f8a072" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-149570/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a6132d06-c0d4-5b9e-9c45-e4dfa26c7569" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-149570/selection/03a4102f13ad3e0ac65ab53676c3f89cede3c650c4dd4e31a2b43a62847e184f" :answer-field/choices ["q-149570/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-149570/selection/d0d01bb2e3e816b9fd6aee47accd74e6df07f3f36fe536db4d7bfbcde2546d68" "q-149570/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" "q-149570/selection/1b562e91f68bc228d59da280605802cc1ce0248d770285443e7d649fb5c75d13" "q-149570/selection/03a4102f13ad3e0ac65ab53676c3f89cede3c650c4dd4e31a2b43a62847e184f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-149570" :question/id #uuid "aedf8fc3-dbed-5730-9f21-b8c81e10ed3e" :question/math-academy-id "q-149570" :question/problem "| **Years in the 1st division ($x$)** | $44$ | $38$ | $32$ | $30$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **Number of Championships ($y$)** | $4$ | $3$ | $3$ | $6$ |\n\nThe table above shows the number of years four English soccer teams have been in the top division and the number of national championships they have won. \nCompute the covariance of the data sets." :question/worked-solution "The (population) covariance of the data sets $x={{x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}}$ and $y={{y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n}}$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}(x,y)=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}),\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i}$ are the means of the data sets.\n\nFirst, we need to compute the means:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{x} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (44+38+32+30) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 144 \\\\  & =36 \\\\ \\overset{―}{y} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (4+3+3+6) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 16 \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the covariance of our data sets is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}(x,y) & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(44\\,-\\,36)(4\\,-\\,4)+(38\\,-\\,36)(3\\,-\\,4)+(32\\,-\\,36)(3\\,-\\,4)+(30\\,-\\,36)(6\\,-\\,4)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(8)(0)+(2)(-1)+(-4)(-1)+(-6)(2)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[0+(-2)+4+(-12)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (-10) \\\\  & =-2.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-149570/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cee807c1-dd86-5b0e-a595-5c5754c47e4c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-149570"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-149571/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "9731e646-5540-52b7-aadd-63a8f615fde4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-149571/selection/1b562e91f68bc228d59da280605802cc1ce0248d770285443e7d649fb5c75d13" :answer/id #uuid "9f7bf132-19c3-5728-baf1-0206f165253f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-149571/selection/d0d01bb2e3e816b9fd6aee47accd74e6df07f3f36fe536db4d7bfbcde2546d68" :answer/id #uuid "40448e8f-a346-5f96-a96a-524ab41d2e54" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-149571/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "926e08ff-1e28-5eb1-a9fc-9ae46a37b025" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-149571/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "ea953bc3-2546-5c6c-819c-fc01fa27e7f5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-149571/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a9b32f33-1de9-5d68-bec4-966608b18422" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-149571/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer-field/choices ["q-149571/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" "q-149571/selection/1b562e91f68bc228d59da280605802cc1ce0248d770285443e7d649fb5c75d13" "q-149571/selection/d0d01bb2e3e816b9fd6aee47accd74e6df07f3f36fe536db4d7bfbcde2546d68" "q-149571/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-149571/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-149571" :question/id #uuid "6ac2ef26-e44c-5f13-aaa3-d7e817fbe704" :question/math-academy-id "q-149571" :question/problem "| **Year of Experience, in years ($x$)** | $1$ | $2$ | $2$ | $7$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **Number of Strikes ($y$)** | $2$ | $1$ | $3$ | $6$ |\n\nFour friends went bowling. The table above shows their years of bowling experience and the number of strikes they got in the game.\nCompute the covariance of the data sets given that the means are $\\overset{―}{x}=3$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=3.$" :question/worked-solution "The (population) covariance of the data sets $x={{x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}}$ and $y={{y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n}}$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}(x,y)=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}),\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i}$ are the means of the data sets.\n\nTherefore, the covariance of our data sets is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}(x,y) & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(1-3)(2-3)+(2-3)(1-3)+(2-3)(3-3)+(7-3)(6-3)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(-2)(-1)+(-1)(-2)+(-1)(0)+(4)(3)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[2+2+0+12] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 16 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-149571/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cee807c1-dd86-5b0e-a595-5c5754c47e4c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-149571"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-149617/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "18724f14-7f52-586e-827c-7cb399c2c942" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-149617/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "58b70067-7d87-53fc-9414-708d983a08e3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-149617/selection/4de395131b8c6206950603752bf3404c42f4dd6f0a41fee38e42388d1b92c133" :answer/id #uuid "3f49453e-af01-583e-8901-3233c603996f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-149617/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "1007fd83-8622-5480-a412-692af3da29a8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-149617/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer/id #uuid "e924e357-dd18-50d8-a41e-f1718ead1747" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-149617/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6a0c7361-5f4e-5202-a29f-f5bce3a55eeb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-149617/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-149617/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" "q-149617/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-149617/selection/4de395131b8c6206950603752bf3404c42f4dd6f0a41fee38e42388d1b92c133" "q-149617/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-149617/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-149617" :question/id #uuid "8c0b0103-1c88-5cc9-84a1-93f9985616e9" :question/math-academy-id "q-149617" :question/problem "Consider the following data sets:\n\n$$\nx={6,\\,4,\\,8,\\,6},\\,y={4,\\,7,\\,11,\\,14}\n$$\n\nYou're given that $\\overset{―}{x}=6$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=9.$ Calculate $\\text{Cov}(x,y).$" :question/worked-solution "The (population) covariance of the data sets $x={{x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}}$ and $y={{y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n}}$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}(x,y)=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}),\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i}$ are the means of the data sets.\n\nTherefore, the covariance of our data sets is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}(x,y) & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(6-6)(4-9)+(4-6)(7-9)+(8-6)(11-9)+(6-6)(14-9)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(0)(-5)+(-2)(-2)+(2)(2)+(0)(5)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[0+4+4+0] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-149617/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a2ac0065-9315-547a-a9cf-c6a5abea1aed"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-149617"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-149618/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "e49fb562-c40b-522c-9967-30b74e5f3889" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-149618/selection/4e2cb386499e1926f074a7bcd422a63175a237204a3823f0fa6c86b56d301873" :answer/id #uuid "29923786-ad5b-56f9-a146-0a084c09261f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-149618/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "8393a22a-eb45-5d8f-9255-47aed91de351" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-149618/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "da956414-cb57-59a4-aa82-33a2a4cc1d25" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-149618/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "d90d32bd-093d-5e5f-90f7-4a91e39b2fed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-149618/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "4367bed7-7046-573e-9881-1ac34861d477" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-149618/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer-field/choices ["q-149618/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" "q-149618/selection/4e2cb386499e1926f074a7bcd422a63175a237204a3823f0fa6c86b56d301873" "q-149618/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" "q-149618/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" "q-149618/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-149618" :question/id #uuid "23453827-8519-5d16-8adc-b4ba457a8582" :question/math-academy-id "q-149618" :question/problem "Calculate $\\text{Cov}(x,y)$ for the following data sets:\n\n$$\nx={-12,\\,-10,\\,-9,\\,-13},\\,y={-2,\\,0,\\,3,\\,3}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The (population) covariance of the data sets $x={{x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}}$ and $y={{y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n}}$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}(x,y)=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}),\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i}$ are the means of the data sets.\n\nFirst, we need to compute the means:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{x} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (-12-10-9-13) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (-44) \\\\  & =-11 \\\\ \\overset{―}{y} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (-2+0+3+3) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the covariance of our data sets is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}(x,y) & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(-12-(-11))(-2-1)+(-10-(-11))(0-1) \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,+(-9-(-11))(3-1)+(-13-(-11))(3-1)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(-1)(-3)+(1)(-1)+(2)(2)+(-2)(2)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[3-1+4-4] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-149618/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a2ac0065-9315-547a-a9cf-c6a5abea1aed"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-149618"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
